Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 3887
Function: xcoff_ppc_relocate_section
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The code computes address = rel->r_vaddr - input_section->vma and only checks if (address > input_section->size) before reading from contents+address. It then reads 2 or 4 bytes via bfd_get_16/bfd_get_32 without ensuring address + reloc_size <= input_section->size. If address is exactly input_section->size or close to it, this results in an out-of-bounds read.

